        <h1>Palermo <em>ZTL</em> map, hours and where to park</h1>
        <p class="lede">Palermo will sell you the right to drive into its old centre. The ZTL covers the historic quarters between the central station and Via Cavour, and between Porta Nuova and Porta Felice on the sea, on weekday daytimes and on Friday and Saturday nights — and any driver in an eligible car can buy a day pass and go in legally. The camera gates work exactly as they do elsewhere in Italy. What is different here is that a wrong turn has a cheap, official remedy, provided you use it in time.</p>
        <p class="byline">
          By <a href="/about">ZTL Italia</a>
          <span class="by-sep">·</span>
          <span>Zone data and guidance last reviewed <time datetime="2026-09-26">26 September 2026</time></span>
        </p>

